# Matomo Analytics

Matomo provides self-hosted, privacy-first product analytics.

This template can scaffold Matomo via Docker Compose when `use_matomo=true`.

## Start Matomo locally

```bash
{{ container_runtime }} compose --profile analytics up -d matomo-db matomo
```

Matomo UI is available at:

- `http://localhost:8082`

## Required environment variables

Set these in `.env` (or `.env.local`) for non-default credentials:

- `MATOMO_DB_ROOT_PASSWORD`
- `MATOMO_DB_NAME`
- `MATOMO_DB_USER`
- `MATOMO_DB_PASSWORD`

## Security recommendations

- Use long random passwords in all environments.
- Expose Matomo behind TLS (Caddy/reverse proxy) in shared environments.
- Restrict network access to analytics services.
- Enable Matomo auto-archiving cron in persistent environments.

## Backup

Persisted volumes:

- `matomo-data` (Matomo app/uploads/plugins state)
- `matomo-db-data` (MariaDB data)

Back up both volumes before upgrades.
